Lab Report : 4

Write a C program to identify whether a given line is a comment or not.





Introduction : 

This C++ program checks whether a user-input line is a comment or not. It prompts the user to enter a line of code and analyzes the beginning of the line after removing leading spaces or tabs. If the line starts with //, it is identified as a single-line comment. If it starts with /*, it is considered the beginning of a multi-line comment. If neither pattern is found, the program concludes that the line is not a comment. This tool is useful for basic syntax checking in source code.

 

Tools :

Here are the tools (components/libraries) used in this C++ program:

1.	#include <iostream>

 – Used for input (cin) and output (cout) operations.

2.	#include <string>

 – Provides the string class and functions like getline(), substr(), and find_first_not_of().

3.	Standard Functions and Features Used:

 – getline(cin, line) to read a full line of user input

 – find_first_not_of() to skip leading spaces or tabs

 – substr() to check the starting characters of the trimmed line

 – Conditional statements (if-else) for logic checking.

 

Source Code : 

#include <iostream>

#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {

    string line;



    cout << "Enter a line of code: ";

    getline(cin, line);



    size_t firstChar = line.find_first_not_of(" \t");



    if (firstChar != string::npos) {

        string trimmedLine = line.substr(firstChar);



        if (trimmedLine.substr(0, 2) == "//") {

            cout << "It is a single-line comment." << endl;

        } else if (trimmedLine.substr(0, 2) == "/*") {

            cout << "It is a multi-line comment start." << endl;

        } else {

            cout << "It is NOT a comment." << endl;

        }

    } else {

        cout << "Empty or whitespace-only line." << endl;

    }



    return 0;

}

